From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi_em: release every radio's AP metrics allocations

ap_report_push_cb() builds one fixed-size VAP report array for every requested
radio.  Its cleanup loop, however, bounds every radio with `radio->vaps.num_vaps`,
where `radio` is merely the last radio visited by the build loop.  When an
earlier radio has more VAPs than the last radio, the link- and traffic-metric
arrays in those additional slots are leaked on every periodic report.

The tri-band EasyMesh layout exposes this deterministically: radio 1 has four
VAPs, radio 2 has three, and AP metrics run every five seconds.  OneWifi PSS
therefore continued growing by roughly 6 MiB/hour even after the encoded
WebConfig buffer ownership fix.

All report slots are zero-initialized, so walk the complete fixed array during
cleanup.  Also send a late invalid-radio failure through that same ownership
boundary; returning directly could retain allocations already prepared for an
earlier radio.

This is a generic OneWifi ownership correction.  It is not hwsim-specific and
matches the complete fixed-array cleanup used by current upstream OneWifi.

Upstream-Status: Backport
---
 source/apps/em/wifi_em.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
index ae8f21f..770b211 100644
--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
@@ -1884,8 +1884,8 @@ static int ap_report_push_cb(em_ap_report_callback_arg_t *args)
         if (radio == NULL) {
             wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_EM, "%s:%d: NULL Pointer of radio_index %d\n", __func__,
                 __LINE__, radio_index);
-            free(data);
-            return RETURN_ERR;
+            rc = RETURN_ERR;
+            goto cleanup;
         }
         vap_map = &radio->vaps.vap_map;
 
@@ -2030,6 +2030,6 @@ cleanup:
     if (data != NULL) {
         for (int j = 0; j < req_radio_count; j++) {
-            for (int i = 0; i < radio->vaps.num_vaps && i < MAX_NUM_VAP_PER_RADIO; i++) {
+            for (int i = 0; i < MAX_NUM_VAP_PER_RADIO; i++) {
                 vap_report = &data->u.decoded.em_ap_metrics_report.radio_reports[j].vap_reports[i];
                 if (vap_report->sta_link_metrics != NULL) {
                     free(vap_report->sta_link_metrics);
